The java.util.concurrent.atomic package was added in Java 5 (JDK 1.5) in 2004 as part of the JSR 166 concurrency 
utilities developed by Doug Lea.

It provides a small toolkit of lock-free, thread-safe programming primitives 
on single variables and arrays using hardware-level Compare-And-Swap (CAS) operations.

Key Features Added in 1.5
Basic Types: AtomicInteger, AtomicLong, AtomicBoolean, and AtomicReference.
Arrays: AtomicIntegerArray, AtomicLongArray, and AtomicReferenceArray.
Field Updaters: AtomicIntegerFieldUpdater, AtomicLongFieldUpdater, and AtomicReferenceFieldUpdater.
Reference State: AtomicStampedReference and AtomicMarkableReference to help solve the ABA problem.

